INSERT INTO events (seq, at, entity, event, detail) VALUES (174, '2026-07-25T19:09:39Z', 'epic:pilot-adaptation', 'criteria', 'met 3: Refreshed 2026-07-25 - the earlier evidence ("one generic defect surfaced (#19)") was true only of the first rehearsals and went stale as the epic continued. The experiments have since filed #22-#24, #26-#32, #34, #36-#47 (verb-surface and import sweeps), #50 (fixture-gate), and #51-#56 (contract gaps found by the deploy re-verification campaign); #57 is an owner question in IN-REVIEW. Fixes applied under this epic carry tests and green gates: the #19 scaffold fix with content tests (be1669e), the terminal-epic guards and R16 with their amendments (a0ac6cc). The remaining filings are open defects deliberately left for later work, which this criterion asks be FILED, not fixed.');
INSERT INTO events (seq, at, entity, event, detail) VALUES (175, '2026-07-25T19:19:27Z', '#40', 'set-status', 'Closed 2026-07-25 as not reproducible. Four data-losing md-table shapes were probed against the binary this task was filed against - an unknown header column, a data row with more cells than the header, a duplicate header column, and known-but-unused columns - and every one is either refused with exit 1 or preserved by folding into note. The header check against a closed per-kind vocabulary sits at internal/verb/import_mdtable.go:242-243 and predates the filing (acdd980, 2026-07-21, four days earlier). Reopen with an exact reproduction if one exists; the silent-no-op defect that IS real for md-table is #39.');
