INSERT INTO events (seq, at, entity, event, detail) VALUES (352, '2026-07-26T10:59:34Z', '#62', 'set-status', 'Closed by story S7 2026-07-26. The criterion text is spelled text on both doors and criterion is an accepted alias on both. criteria add takes --text and --criterion as one flag rather than as a flag plus a better error, because an undefined flag dies in the dispatcher''s flag.Parse before any verb body runs - the mistyped spelling can be given a meaning but never a message. Supplying both with different values is a usage refusal on both surfaces, which is what obliges the corpus''s decoded fields to distinguish absent from present-and-empty; the verb resolves which flag was typed by fs.Visit, so --text '''' counts as present. Both refusals name the other spelling. Verified by the coordinating agent against a throwaway tracker: --text and --criterion write the same criteria list; both flags with different values refuse usage; neither flag refuses naming both; a corpus using text imports, one using criterion imports, one using both with different values refuses, and a third guess is redirected to both accepted names. The DDL is byte-equal before and after, sha 8bbb8daec5f8347b from binaries built at HEAD and at this tree, so no dump migrates and the schema version does not move.');
INSERT INTO events (seq, at, entity, event, detail) VALUES (353, '2026-07-26T10:59:54Z', 'epic:adoption-contract/S7', 'story', 'done: 0508e92..8bf79be; gate: make gates exit 0 (build, vet, test -race all packages, golangci-lint 0 issues, fix-check clean, govulncheck clean, check-pins, check-copies, binaries); selftracked verify full: 0 violations. DDL byte-equality verified independently by the coordinating agent: binaries built from HEAD and from this tree emit an identical DDL block, sha 8bbb8daec5f8347b both.');
